  user_input {
    user_response: "User prompt: # Build a Dummy Staff Location Attendance Web App\n\nCreate a complete **dummy web application for staff location-based attendance/presence tracking** for **Rajalakshmi Institute of Technology (RIT)**.\n\nThe application is only a prototype/demo for now. Do NOT implement real user registration, database authentication, payment systems, or production security. Use dummy credentials and local storage/file-based storage where appropriate.\n\n## 1. Main Concept\n\nThe system has two types of users:\n\n### Staff\n\nA staff member:\n\n1. Logs in using a dummy Staff ID and password.\n2. Is taken to a staff dashboard.\n3. The dashboard contains **ONLY ONE main button**: `PUSH`\n4. The staff member can press the button **only once**.\n5. Once pressed:\n\n   * The browser requests the user\'s GPS location.\n   * Get the current latitude and longitude.\n   * Determine which campus block/place the person is currently inside.\n   * If the coordinates fall inside one of the defined campus areas, store that place name.\n   * If the coordinates do not fall inside any defined area, store `Outside`.\n   * Record the exact timestamp when the button was pressed.\n   * Store the Staff ID, timestamp, latitude, longitude, and detected location.\n6. After pressing the button, disable the button permanently for that session and visually change it to something like:\n   `PUSHED`\n7. The staff must not be able to press it again through the normal UI.\n\n### Admin\n\nCreate a separate **Admin Login** page.\n\nOnly the admin should be able to access the attendance/location records.\n\nThe admin should be able to:\n\n* Log in using a dummy admin username/password.\n* View the recorded staff entries.\n* Download/export the records as an **Excel (.xlsx) file**.\n\nThe Excel sheet must contain at minimum:\n\n| Staff ID | Timestamp           | Latitude | Longitude | Location        |\n| -------- | ------------------- | -------- | --------- | --------------- |\n| STAFF001 | 2026-09-02 21:45:32 | 13.xxxxx | 80.xxxxx  | A / Admin Block |\n\nThe `Location` column should contain the campus place name, or `Outside`.\n\n---\n\n# 2. Dummy Login Credentials\n\nUse hardcoded dummy credentials for this prototype.\n\n### Staff\n\nStaff ID:\n`STAFF001`\n\nPassword:\n`staff123`\n\nOptionally allow a few additional dummy staff accounts such as:\n\n`STAFF002 / staff123`\n\n`STAFF003 / staff123`\n\n### Admin\n\nUsername:\n`admin`\n\nPassword:\n`admin123`\n\nClearly label these as **DEMO / DUMMY CREDENTIALS** in the project.\n\n---\n\n# 3. Campus Geofencing Coordinates\n\nUse the following coordinate ranges from the supplied RIT Campus Coordinate Ranges PDF.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nThe format is:\n\n**Longitude X \342\206\222 Y | Latitude A \342\206\222 B**\n\nTherefore:\n\n```text\nlongitude_min <= current_longitude <= longitude_max\nAND\nlatitude_min <= current_latitude <= latitude_max\n```\n\nshould initially be used to determine whether a coordinate falls inside a location.\n\n## A / Admin Block\n\nLongitude:\n\n```text\n80.0452290 \342\206\222 80.0457286\n```\n\nLatitude:\n\n```text\n13.0381506 \342\206\222 13.0386278\n```\n\nStore the location as:\n\n```text\nA / Admin Block\n```\n\n---\n\n## B Block\n\nLongitude:\n\n```text\n80.0448116 \342\206\222 80.0450932\n```\n\nLatitude:\n\n```text\n13.0386850 \342\206\222 13.0394490\n```\n\nStore the location as:\n\n```text\nB Block\n```\n\n---\n\n## C Blocks (C1\342\200\223C4)\n\nLongitude:\n\n```text\n80.0454785 \342\206\222 80.0459096\n```\n\nLatitude:\n\n```text\n13.0388561 \342\206\222 13.0399281\n```\n\nStore the location as:\n\n```text\nC Blocks (C1\342\200\223C4)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Steve Jobs\n\nLongitude:\n\n```text\n80.0445206 \342\206\222 80.0448954\n```\n\nLatitude:\n\n```text\n13.0395535 \342\206\222 13.0398507\n```\n\nStore the location as:\n\n```text\nSteve Jobs\n```\n\n---\n\n## Green Building\n\nLongitude:\n\n```text\n80.0447137 \342\206\222 80.0450191\n```\n\nLatitude:\n\n```text\n13.0377332 \342\206\222 13.0381709\n```\n\nStore the location as:\n\n```text\nGreen Building\n```\n\n---\n\n## Invisible Statue\n\nLongitude:\n\n```text\n80.0449631 \342\206\222 80.0452458\n```\n\nLatitude:\n\n```text\n13.0396760 \342\206\222 13.0403240\n```\n\nStore the location as:\n\n```text\nInvisible Statue\n```\n\n---\n\n## Canteen (Bill Counter)\n\nLongitude:\n\n```text\n80.0453383 \342\206\222 80.0454868\n```\n\nLatitude:\n\n```text\n13.0399611 \342\206\222 13.0403701\n```\n\nStore the location as:\n\n```text\nCanteen (Bill Counter)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Canteen (Calcutta Box)\n\nLongitude:\n\n```text\n80.0452012 \342\206\222 80.0453752\n```\n\nLatitude:\n\n```text\n13.0403335 \342\206\222 13.0405236\n```\n\nStore the location as:\n\n```text\nCanteen (Calcutta Box)\n```\n\nThese ranges are derived from the supplied KML. The PDF notes that the original KML polygon is more precise than simple bounding ranges, so structure the geofencing code in a way that allows the bounding-box method to later be replaced by a **point-in-polygon check** without rewriting the rest of the application.\n\n---\n\n# 4. Location Detection Logic\n\nWhen the staff clicks `PUSH`:\n\nUse the browser Geolocation API:\n\n```javascript\nnavigator.geolocation.getCurrentPosition(...)\n```\n\nObtain:\n\n```text\nlatitude\nlongitude\n```\n\nThen run:\n\n```text\ndetectLocation(latitude, longitude)\n```\n\nThe function should check the coordinate against all campus ranges.\n\nPseudo-logic:\n\n```text\nIF coordinate is inside A / Admin Block\n    location = \"A / Admin Block\"\n\nELSE IF coordinate is inside B Block\n    location = \"B Block\"\n\nELSE IF coordinate is inside C Blocks\n    location = \"C Blocks (C1\342\200\223C4)\"\n\nELSE IF coordinate is inside Steve Jobs\n    location = \"Steve Jobs\"\n\nELSE IF coordinate is inside Green Building\n    location = \"Green Building\"\n\nELSE IF coordinate is inside Invisible Statue\n    location = \"Invisible Statue\"\n\nELSE IF coordinate is inside Canteen (Bill Counter)\n    location = \"Canteen (Bill Counter)\"\n\nELSE IF coordinate is inside Canteen (Calcutta Box)\n    location = \"Canteen (Calcutta Box)\"\n\nELSE\n    location = \"Outside\"\n```\n\n---\n\n# 5. Important Overlapping Boundary Handling\n\nSome campus bounding ranges may overlap.\n\nDo NOT silently assume that bounding boxes perfectly represent the actual building boundaries.\n\nCreate the location detection function as a separate module/function, for example:\n\n```text\ngeofence.js\n```\n\nor, if using Python:\n\n```text\ngeofence.py\n```\n\nso that the actual KML polygons can later be inserted.\n\nFor this dummy prototype, use the supplied coordinate ranges.\n\nIf a coordinate falls into more than one bounding range, use a clearly defined priority order and keep that priority in one configuration array so it can easily be changed later.\n\n---\n\n# 6. Staff Page UI\n\nAfter successful staff login, show a very simple page.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\n--------------------------------\n\n        STAFF PRESENCE\n\n        Staff ID: STAFF001\n\n        [ PUSH ]\n\n--------------------------------\n```\n\nThe page should intentionally be minimal.\n\nBefore pressing:\n\n```text\n[PUSH]\n```\n\nAfter pressing:\n\n```text\n[PUSHED]\n```\n\nThe button must become disabled:\n\n```html\n<button disabled>PUSHED</button>\n```\n\nAlso show a small status message:\n\n```text\nLocation detected: A / Admin Block\nTime recorded: 02 Sep 2026, 09:45 PM\n```\n\nDo NOT show the coordinates prominently on the staff page unless useful for debugging.\n\n---\n\n# 7. Prevent Multiple Pushes\n\nThe frontend should immediately disable the button after the first click.\n\nAlso implement a backend/server-side check.\n\nDo NOT rely only on:\n\n```javascript\nbutton.disabled = true\n```\n\nbecause the browser can be manipulated.\n\nFor this dummy application, maintain a record that the logged-in staff member has already pushed.\n\nIf they try to send another push request:\n\n```text\nPush already recorded for this staff member.\n```\n\nDo not create another Excel row.\n\nFor the prototype, the state can be stored using a local JSON file or SQLite database.\n\n---\n\n# 8. Excel Storage\n\nEvery successful push should create one attendance/presence record.\n\nUse Python `openpyxl` if the backend is Python.\n\nExcel file:\n\n```text\nstaff_presence.xlsx\n```\n\nColumns:\n\n```text\nStaff ID\nTimestamp\nLatitude\nLongitude\nLocation\n```\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nSTAFF001 | 2026-09-02 21:45:32 | 13.0384 | 80.0454 | A / Admin Block\nSTAFF002 | 2026-09-02 21:51:07 | 13.0391 | 80.0449 | B Block\nSTAFF003 | 2026-09-02 21:54:12 | 13.0412 | 80.0461 | Outside\n```\n\nCreate the Excel file automatically if it does not exist.\n\nDo not overwrite previous records.\n\nAppend new records.\n\n---\n\n# 9. Admin Dashboard\n\nCreate:\n\n```text\n/admin/login\n```\n\nand:\n\n```text\n/admin/dashboard\n```\n\nThe admin dashboard should display:\n\n```text\nADMIN DASHBOARD\n\nStaff Presence Records\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------\nStaff ID | Timestamp | Latitude | Longitude | Location\n--------------------------------------------------------------\nSTAFF001 | ...        | ...      | ...       | A / Admin Block\nSTAFF002 | ...        | ...      | ...       | Outside\n--------------------------------------------------------------\n\n[ Download Excel ]\n```\n\nThe admin should be able to download:\n\n```text\nstaff_presence.xlsx\n```\n\nThe Excel file must contain all recorded entries.\n\n---\n\n# 10. Admin Access Restriction\n\nStaff must NOT be able to access the admin dashboard.\n\nImplement a basic session-based authentication system.\n\nFor example:\n\n```text\nstaff_logged_in = true\nadmin_logged_in = true\n```\n\nThe admin routes must verify that the user is logged in as admin.\n\nIf a staff member tries:\n\n```text\n/admin/dashboard\n```\n\nredirect them to:\n\n```text\n/admin/login\n```\n\nDo not expose the Excel file through a publicly accessible static folder.\n\nThe Excel file should only be downloadable through an authenticated admin endpoint.\n\n---\n\n# 11. Recommended Technology\n\nBuild this as a simple full-stack application.\n\nPreferred stack:\n\n### Backend\n\n```text\nPython\nFlask\nopenpyxl\n```\n\n### Frontend\n\n```text\nHTML\nCSS\nJavaScript\nBootstrap\n```\n\n### Storage\n\nFor this dummy version:\n\n```text\nSQLite or JSON\n```\n\nfor login/push state, plus:\n\n```text\nstaff_presence.xlsx\n```\n\nfor the exported attendance records.\n\nKeep the architecture simple and beginner-friendly.\n\n---\n\n# 12. Suggested Project Structure\n\nCreate:\n\n```text\nstaff-location-app/\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 app.py\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 geofence.py\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 requirements.txt\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 data/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 staff_presence.xlsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 app.db\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 templates/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 login.html\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 staff_dashboard.html\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 admin_login.html\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 admin_dashboard.html\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 static/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 css/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 style.css\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 js/\n\342\224\202       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 staff.js\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 README.md\n```\n\n---\n\n# 13. Error Handling\n\nHandle these cases properly.\n\n### Location permission denied\n\nDisplay:\n\n```text\nLocation permission is required to record your presence.\nPlease enable location access and try again.\n```\n\nThe push should NOT be recorded if the location cannot be obtained.\n\n### GPS unavailable\n\nDisplay:\n\n```text\nUnable to determine your location. Please try again.\n```\n\n### Outside campus/buildings\n\nThis is a valid result.\n\nDisplay:\n\n```text\nLocation detected: Outside\n```\n\nand save:\n\n```text\nOutside\n```\n\nto Excel.\n\n### Already pushed\n\nDisplay:\n\n```text\nYour presence has already been recorded.\n```\n\n---\n\n# 14. Timestamp\n\nGenerate the timestamp on the backend when the push request is received.\n\nUse a readable format:\n\n```text\nYYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS\n```\n\nExample:\n\n```text\n2026-09-02 21:45:32\n```\n\nDo not trust a timestamp sent by the frontend.\n\n---\n\n# 15. Security for the Dummy Version\n\nThis is only a prototype, but still follow basic good practices:\n\n* Do not put the Excel file in the public/static directory.\n* Do not expose admin credentials in the admin dashboard.\n* Use sessions for login state.\n* Validate Staff IDs.\n* Validate latitude and longitude.\n* Only authenticated admin users can download Excel.\n* Prevent duplicate push records.\n* Do not allow arbitrary file paths in download requests.\n\nClearly comment that the hardcoded credentials are **for demonstration only** and must be replaced with proper authentication in a real deployment.\n\n---\n\n# 16. UI Design\n\nMake the interface clean and professional but simple.\n\nUse a campus/administrative dashboard aesthetic.\n\nStaff page should focus almost entirely on the single PUSH button.\n\nAdmin page should look like a simple data-management dashboard.\n\nMake it responsive for:\n\n* Desktop\n* Tablet\n* Mobile\n\n---\n\n# 17. Important Prototype Behavior\n\nThe complete workflow should be:\n\n```text\n                \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n                \342\224\202   Staff Login   \342\224\202\n                \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n                         \342\224\202\n                         \342\226\274\n                \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n                \342\224\202 Staff Dashboard \342\224\202\n                \342\224\202                 \342\224\202\n                \342\224\202     [ PUSH ]    \342\224\202\n                \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n                         \342\224\202\n                         \342\226\274\n                Get Browser GPS\n                         \342\224\202\n                         \342\226\274\n              latitude + longitude\n                         \342\224\202\n                         \342\226\274\n                 Geofence Check\n                         \342\224\202\n          \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\264\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n          \342\224\202                             \342\224\202\n          \342\226\274                             \342\226\274\n    Inside a defined area          No matching area\n          \342\224\202                             \342\224\202\n          \342\226\274                             \342\226\274\n    Store block name                 \"Outside\"\n          \342\224\202                             \342\224\202\n          \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n                         \342\224\202\n                         \342\226\274\n                Record timestamp\n                         \342\224\202\n                         \342\226\274\n                   Save record\n                         \342\224\202\n                         \342\226\274\n                Excel (.xlsx)\n                         \342\224\202\n                         \342\226\274\n                  Admin Dashboard\n                         \342\224\202\n                         \342\226\274\n                  Download Excel\n```\n\n---\n\n# 18. Deliverables\n\nGenerate the complete working project.\n\nI should be able to run:\n\n```bash\npip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n\nthen:\n\n```bash\npython app.py\n```\n\nand open the application locally.\n\nProvide:\n\n1. Complete Flask backend\n2. Complete HTML templates\n3. CSS\n4. JavaScript\n5. Geofencing logic\n6. Excel generation/export\n7. Dummy staff authentication\n8. Dummy admin authentication\n9. Session handling\n10. Duplicate push prevention\n11. GPS location detection\n12. Campus coordinate configuration\n13. Admin-only Excel access\n14. README with exact setup and run instructions\n\nDo not leave placeholders such as:\n\n```text\n// implement this later\n```\n\nor:\n\n```text\nTODO\n```\n\nThe application should be runnable immediately as a **dummy prototype**.\n\n## Coordinate Source Note\n\nThe campus coordinate ranges above are taken from the supplied **RIT Campus Coordinate Ranges** PDF. The source describes them as KML-derived bounding ranges and explicitly notes that the original KML polygon is more precise than a simple coordinate range; therefore, keep the geofencing implementation modular so the actual KML polygons can be substituted later for more accurate point-in-polygon detection.\n\n\nHere is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/public/assets/aistudio/.gitignore\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.1.14\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^5.0.4\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^6.2.3\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.1.14\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ~5.8.2\nvite: ^6.2.3\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {StrictMode} from \'react\';\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(\n  <StrictMode>\n    <App />\n  </StrictMode>,\n);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\303\242\302\200\302\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
    items {
      text: "User prompt: # Build a Dummy Staff Location Attendance Web App\n\nCreate a complete **dummy web application for staff location-based attendance/presence tracking** for **Rajalakshmi Institute of Technology (RIT)**.\n\nThe application is only a prototype/demo for now. Do NOT implement real user registration, database authentication, payment systems, or production security. Use dummy credentials and local storage/file-based storage where appropriate.\n\n## 1. Main Concept\n\nThe system has two types of users:\n\n### Staff\n\nA staff member:\n\n1. Logs in using a dummy Staff ID and password.\n2. Is taken to a staff dashboard.\n3. The dashboard contains **ONLY ONE main button**: `PUSH`\n4. The staff member can press the button **only once**.\n5. Once pressed:\n\n   * The browser requests the user\'s GPS location.\n   * Get the current latitude and longitude.\n   * Determine which campus block/place the person is currently inside.\n   * If the coordinates fall inside one of the defined campus areas, store that place name.\n   * If the coordinates do not fall inside any defined area, store `Outside`.\n   * Record the exact timestamp when the button was pressed.\n   * Store the Staff ID, timestamp, latitude, longitude, and detected location.\n6. After pressing the button, disable the button permanently for that session and visually change it to something like:\n   `PUSHED`\n7. The staff must not be able to press it again through the normal UI.\n\n### Admin\n\nCreate a separate **Admin Login** page.\n\nOnly the admin should be able to access the attendance/location records.\n\nThe admin should be able to:\n\n* Log in using a dummy admin username/password.\n* View the recorded staff entries.\n* Download/export the records as an **Excel (.xlsx) file**.\n\nThe Excel sheet must contain at minimum:\n\n| Staff ID | Timestamp           | Latitude | Longitude | Location        |\n| -------- | ------------------- | -------- | --------- | --------------- |\n| STAFF001 | 2026-09-02 21:45:32 | 13.xxxxx | 80.xxxxx  | A / Admin Block |\n\nThe `Location` column should contain the campus place name, or `Outside`.\n\n---\n\n# 2. Dummy Login Credentials\n\nUse hardcoded dummy credentials for this prototype.\n\n### Staff\n\nStaff ID:\n`STAFF001`\n\nPassword:\n`staff123`\n\nOptionally allow a few additional dummy staff accounts such as:\n\n`STAFF002 / staff123`\n\n`STAFF003 / staff123`\n\n### Admin\n\nUsername:\n`admin`\n\nPassword:\n`admin123`\n\nClearly label these as **DEMO / DUMMY CREDENTIALS** in the project.\n\n---\n\n# 3. Campus Geofencing Coordinates\n\nUse the following coordinate ranges from the supplied RIT Campus Coordinate Ranges PDF.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nThe format is:\n\n**Longitude X \342\206\222 Y | Latitude A \342\206\222 B**\n\nTherefore:\n\n```text\nlongitude_min <= current_longitude <= longitude_max\nAND\nlatitude_min <= current_latitude <= latitude_max\n```\n\nshould initially be used to determine whether a coordinate falls inside a location.\n\n## A / Admin Block\n\nLongitude:\n\n```text\n80.0452290 \342\206\222 80.0457286\n```\n\nLatitude:\n\n```text\n13.0381506 \342\206\222 13.0386278\n```\n\nStore the location as:\n\n```text\nA / Admin Block\n```\n\n---\n\n## B Block\n\nLongitude:\n\n```text\n80.0448116 \342\206\222 80.0450932\n```\n\nLatitude:\n\n```text\n13.0386850 \342\206\222 13.0394490\n```\n\nStore the location as:\n\n```text\nB Block\n```\n\n---\n\n## C Blocks (C1\342\200\223C4)\n\nLongitude:\n\n```text\n80.0454785 \342\206\222 80.0459096\n```\n\nLatitude:\n\n```text\n13.0388561 \342\206\222 13.0399281\n```\n\nStore the location as:\n\n```text\nC Blocks (C1\342\200\223C4)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Steve Jobs\n\nLongitude:\n\n```text\n80.0445206 \342\206\222 80.0448954\n```\n\nLatitude:\n\n```text\n13.0395535 \342\206\222 13.0398507\n```\n\nStore the location as:\n\n```text\nSteve Jobs\n```\n\n---\n\n## Green Building\n\nLongitude:\n\n```text\n80.0447137 \342\206\222 80.0450191\n```\n\nLatitude:\n\n```text\n13.0377332 \342\206\222 13.0381709\n```\n\nStore the location as:\n\n```text\nGreen Building\n```\n\n---\n\n## Invisible Statue\n\nLongitude:\n\n```text\n80.0449631 \342\206\222 80.0452458\n```\n\nLatitude:\n\n```text\n13.0396760 \342\206\222 13.0403240\n```\n\nStore the location as:\n\n```text\nInvisible Statue\n```\n\n---\n\n## Canteen (Bill Counter)\n\nLongitude:\n\n```text\n80.0453383 \342\206\222 80.0454868\n```\n\nLatitude:\n\n```text\n13.0399611 \342\206\222 13.0403701\n```\n\nStore the location as:\n\n```text\nCanteen (Bill Counter)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Canteen (Calcutta Box)\n\nLongitude:\n\n```text\n80.0452012 \342\206\222 80.0453752\n```\n\nLatitude:\n\n```text\n13.0403335 \342\206\222 13.0405236\n```\n\nStore the location as:\n\n```text\nCanteen (Calcutta Box)\n```\n\nThese ranges are derived from the supplied KML. The PDF notes that the original KML polygon is more precise than simple bounding ranges, so structure the geofencing code in a way that allows the bounding-box method to later be replaced by a **point-in-polygon check** without rewriting the rest of the application.\n\n---\n\n# 4. Location Detection Logic\n\nWhen the staff clicks `PUSH`:\n\nUse the browser Geolocation API:\n\n```javascript\nnavigator.geolocation.getCurrentPosition(...)\n```\n\nObtain:\n\n```text\nlatitude\nlongitude\n```\n\nThen run:\n\n```text\ndetectLocation(latitude, longitude)\n```\n\nThe function should check the coordinate against all campus ranges.\n\nPseudo-logic:\n\n```text\nIF coordinate is inside A / Admin Block\n    location = \"A / Admin Block\"\n\nELSE IF coordinate is inside B Block\n    location = \"B Block\"\n\nELSE IF coordinate is inside C Blocks\n    location = \"C Blocks (C1\342\200\223C4)\"\n\nELSE IF coordinate is inside Steve Jobs\n    location = \"Steve Jobs\"\n\nELSE IF coordinate is inside Green Building\n    location = \"Green Building\"\n\nELSE IF coordinate is inside Invisible Statue\n    location = \"Invisible Statue\"\n\nELSE IF coordinate is inside Canteen (Bill Counter)\n    location = \"Canteen (Bill Counter)\"\n\nELSE IF coordinate is inside Canteen (Calcutta Box)\n    location = \"Canteen (Calcutta Box)\"\n\nELSE\n    location = \"Outside\"\n```\n\n---\n\n# 5. Important Overlapping Boundary Handling\n\nSome campus bounding ranges may overlap.\n\nDo NOT silently assume that bounding boxes perfectly represent the actual building boundaries.\n\nCreate the location detection function as a separate module/function, for example:\n\n```text\ngeofence.js\n```\n\nor, if using Python:\n\n```text\ngeofence.py\n```\n\nso that the actual KML polygons can later be inserted.\n\nFor this dummy prototype, use the supplied coordinate ranges.\n\nIf a coordinate falls into more than one bounding range, use a clearly defined priority order and keep that priority in one configuration array so it can easily be changed later.\n\n---\n\n# 6. Staff Page UI\n\nAfter successful staff login, show a very simple page.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\n--------------------------------\n\n        STAFF PRESENCE\n\n        Staff ID: STAFF001\n\n        [ PUSH ]\n\n--------------------------------\n```\n\nThe page should intentionally be minimal.\n\nBefore pressing:\n\n```text\n[PUSH]\n```\n\nAfter pressing:\n\n```text\n[PUSHED]\n```\n\nThe button must become disabled:\n\n```html\n<button disabled>PUSHED</button>\n```\n\nAlso show a small status message:\n\n```text\nLocation detected: A / Admin Block\nTime recorded: 02 Sep 2026, 09:45 PM\n```\n\nDo NOT show the coordinates prominently on the staff page unless useful for debugging.\n\n---\n\n# 7. Prevent Multiple Pushes\n\nThe frontend should immediately disable the button after the first click.\n\nAlso implement a backend/server-side check.\n\nDo NOT rely only on:\n\n```javascript\nbutton.disabled = true\n```\n\nbecause the browser can be manipulated.\n\nFor this dummy application, maintain a record that the logged-in staff member has already pushed.\n\nIf they try to send another push request:\n\n```text\nPush already recorded for this staff member.\n```\n\nDo not create another Excel row.\n\nFor the prototype, the state can be stored using a local JSON file or SQLite database.\n\n---\n\n# 8. Excel Storage\n\nEvery successful push should create one attendance/presence record.\n\nUse Python `openpyxl` if the backend is Python.\n\nExcel file:\n\n```text\nstaff_presence.xlsx\n```\n\nColumns:\n\n```text\nStaff ID\nTimestamp\nLatitude\nLongitude\nLocation\n```\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nSTAFF001 | 2026-09-02 21:45:32 | 13.0384 | 80.0454 | A / Admin Block\nSTAFF002 | 2026-09-02 21:51:07 | 13.0391 | 80.0449 | B Block\nSTAFF003 | 2026-09-02 21:54:12 | 13.0412 | 80.0461 | Outside\n```\n\nCreate the Excel file automatically if it does not exist.\n\nDo not overwrite previous records.\n\nAppend new records.\n\n---\n\n# 9. Admin Dashboard\n\nCreate:\n\n```text\n/admin/login\n```\n\nand:\n\n```text\n/admin/dashboard\n```\n\nThe admin dashboard should display:\n\n```text\nADMIN DASHBOARD\n\nStaff Presence Records\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------\nStaff ID | Timestamp | Latitude | Longitude | Location\n--------------------------------------------------------------\nSTAFF001 | ...        | ...      | ...       | A / Admin Block\nSTAFF002 | ...        | ...      | ...       | Outside\n--------------------------------------------------------------\n\n[ Download Excel ]\n```\n\nThe admin should be able to download:\n\n```text\nstaff_presence.xlsx\n```\n\nThe Excel file must contain all recorded entries.\n\n---\n\n# 10. Admin Access Restriction\n\nStaff must NOT be able to access the admin dashboard.\n\nImplement a basic session-based authentication system.\n\nFor example:\n\n```text\nstaff_logged_in = true\nadmin_logged_in = true\n```\n\nThe admin routes must verify that the user is logged in as admin.\n\nIf a staff member tries:\n\n```text\n/admin/dashboard\n```\n\nredirect them to:\n\n```text\n/admin/login\n```\n\nDo not expose the Excel file through a publicly accessible static folder.\n\nThe Excel file should only be downloadable through an authenticated admin endpoint.\n\n---\n\n# 11. Recommended Technology\n\nBuild this as a simple full-stack application.\n\nPreferred stack:\n\n### Backend\n\n```text\nPython\nFlask\nopenpyxl\n```\n\n### Frontend\n\n```text\nHTML\nCSS\nJavaScript\nBootstrap\n```\n\n### Storage\n\nFor this dummy version:\n\n```text\nSQLite or JSON\n```\n\nfor login/push state, plus:\n\n```text\nstaff_presence.xlsx\n```\n\nfor the exported attendance records.\n\nKeep the architecture simple and beginner-friendly.\n\n---\n\n# 12. Suggested Project Structure\n\nCreate:\n\n```text\nstaff-location-app/\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 app.py\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 geofence.py\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 requirements.txt\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 data/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 staff_presence.xlsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 app.db\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 templates/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 login.html\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 staff_dashboard.html\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 admin_login.html\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 admin_dashboard.html\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 static/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 css/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 style.css\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 js/\n\342\224\202       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 staff.js\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 README.md\n```\n\n---\n\n# 13. Error Handling\n\nHandle these cases properly.\n\n### Location permission denied\n\nDisplay:\n\n```text\nLocation permission is required to record your presence.\nPlease enable location access and try again.\n```\n\nThe push should NOT be recorded if the location cannot be obtained.\n\n### GPS unavailable\n\nDisplay:\n\n```text\nUnable to determine your location. Please try again.\n```\n\n### Outside campus/buildings\n\nThis is a valid result.\n\nDisplay:\n\n```text\nLocation detected: Outside\n```\n\nand save:\n\n```text\nOutside\n```\n\nto Excel.\n\n### Already pushed\n\nDisplay:\n\n```text\nYour presence has already been recorded.\n```\n\n---\n\n# 14. Timestamp\n\nGenerate the timestamp on the backend when the push request is received.\n\nUse a readable format:\n\n```text\nYYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS\n```\n\nExample:\n\n```text\n2026-09-02 21:45:32\n```\n\nDo not trust a timestamp sent by the frontend.\n\n---\n\n# 15. Security for the Dummy Version\n\nThis is only a prototype, but still follow basic good practices:\n\n* Do not put the Excel file in the public/static directory.\n* Do not expose admin credentials in the admin dashboard.\n* Use sessions for login state.\n* Validate Staff IDs.\n* Validate latitude and longitude.\n* Only authenticated admin users can download Excel.\n* Prevent duplicate push records.\n* Do not allow arbitrary file paths in download requests.\n\nClearly comment that the hardcoded credentials are **for demonstration only** and must be replaced with proper authentication in a real deployment.\n\n---\n\n# 16. UI Design\n\nMake the interface clean and professional but simple.\n\nUse a campus/administrative dashboard aesthetic.\n\nStaff page should focus almost entirely on the single PUSH button.\n\nAdmin page should look like a simple data-management dashboard.\n\nMake it responsive for:\n\n* Desktop\n* Tablet\n* Mobile\n\n---\n\n# 17. Important Prototype Behavior\n\nThe complete workflow should be:\n\n```text\n                \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n                \342\224\202   Staff Login   \342\224\202\n                \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n                         \342\224\202\n                         \342\226\274\n                \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n                \342\224\202 Staff Dashboard \342\224\202\n                \342\224\202                 \342\224\202\n                \342\224\202     [ PUSH ]    \342\224\202\n                \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n                         \342\224\202\n                         \342\226\274\n                Get Browser GPS\n                         \342\224\202\n                         \342\226\274\n              latitude + longitude\n                         \342\224\202\n                         \342\226\274\n                 Geofence Check\n                         \342\224\202\n          \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\264\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n          \342\224\202                             \342\224\202\n          \342\226\274                             \342\226\274\n    Inside a defined area          No matching area\n          \342\224\202                             \342\224\202\n          \342\226\274                             \342\226\274\n    Store block name                 \"Outside\"\n          \342\224\202                             \342\224\202\n          \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n                         \342\224\202\n                         \342\226\274\n                Record timestamp\n                         \342\224\202\n                         \342\226\274\n                   Save record\n                         \342\224\202\n                         \342\226\274\n                Excel (.xlsx)\n                         \342\224\202\n                         \342\226\274\n                  Admin Dashboard\n                         \342\224\202\n                         \342\226\274\n                  Download Excel\n```\n\n---\n\n# 18. Deliverables\n\nGenerate the complete working project.\n\nI should be able to run:\n\n```bash\npip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n\nthen:\n\n```bash\npython app.py\n```\n\nand open the application locally.\n\nProvide:\n\n1. Complete Flask backend\n2. Complete HTML templates\n3. CSS\n4. JavaScript\n5. Geofencing logic\n6. Excel generation/export\n7. Dummy staff authentication\n8. Dummy admin authentication\n9. Session handling\n10. Duplicate push prevention\n11. GPS location detection\n12. Campus coordinate configuration\n13. Admin-only Excel access\n14. README with exact setup and run instructions\n\nDo not leave placeholders such as:\n\n```text\n// implement this later\n```\n\nor:\n\n```text\nTODO\n```\n\nThe application should be runnable immediately as a **dummy prototype**.\n\n## Coordinate Source Note\n\nThe campus coordinate ranges above are taken from the supplied **RIT Campus Coordinate Ranges** PDF. The source describes them as KML-derived bounding ranges and explicitly notes that the original KML polygon is more precise than a simple coordinate range; therefore, keep the geofencing implementation modular so the actual KML polygons can be substituted later for more accurate point-in-polygon detection.\n\n\nHere is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/public/assets/aistudio/.gitignore\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.1.14\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^5.0.4\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^6.2.3\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.1.14\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ~5.8.2\nvite: ^6.2.3\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {StrictMode} from \'react\';\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(\n  <StrictMode>\n    <App />\n  </StrictMode>,\n);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\303\242\302\200\302\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
    }
  }
}
