  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Prompt\'s Details**\n\nI\'m digging into the specifics of this project now. It looks like it needs to be a dummy staff location attendance web app specifically for Rajalakshmi Institute of Technology (RIT), focusing on staff flow. The key seems to be a simulation, not a real-time tracking system.\n\n\n**Defining App Functionality**\n\nI\'ve got a clearer picture of the app\'s features. Staff can log in, push a button to record their location and time, which triggers GPS, and then identifies their location on campus. An admin dashboard is planned for viewing and exporting staff data. Also, it is a Node/Express/React/Vite TypeScript environment!\n\n\n**Reconciling Tech Stack**\n\nI\'m now grappling with the technology choices. The initial prompt suggests Python/Flask, but the environment leans heavily toward Node.js, Express, and React. There\'s a conflict between the requirements, and I\'m figuring out if I can reconcile this by providing a Node/Express app as per environment constraints. It has to run on port 3000, as the iframe requires!\n\n\n"
