  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Initiating Application Design**\n\nOkay, I\'m starting to build a web app for staff attendance at RIT, as requested. The core of this dummy application will focus on location-based presence tracking. Right now I am thinking about how to get the basic architecture started.\n\n\n**Refining Scope Definition**\n\nI\'ve decided to maintain the prototype/demo scope for the web app, avoiding real user registration, payment systems, and production security features. Dummy credentials and local storage will be used. Moreover, I\'m integrating Google Sheets synchronization and Excel export capabilities into the plan. The system will use the user\'s Google account for authentication to allow updating Google Sheets.\n\n\n**Integrating Dependencies & Frameworks**\n\nI\'m now incorporating necessary npm packages like `firebase` for authentication and `xlsx` for Excel generation. The project structure will include a Flask backend with the requested files, allowing users to run `pip install -r requirements.txt` followed by `python app.py`. I\'m also ensuring the React/Express web application runs on port 3000 within the browser/AI Studio container. This will deliver all the deliverables requested, including HTML, CSS, JavaScript, geofencing, Excel export, and dummy authentication.\n\n\n**Implementing Geofencing Logic**\n\nI\'m now incorporating detailed geofencing rules for precise location verification within the RIT campus. The design includes specific coordinates for various blocks and landmarks, ensuring accurate presence detection via GPS, including custom GPS simulation for testing and default real geolocation. Staff and Admin login are configured.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 331710043
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
