steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1788366470
      nanos: 75757500
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "# Build a Simple Dummy Staff Push & Location Tracking Web App\n\nCreate a simple full-stack prototype web application for staff presence tracking at Rajalakshmi Institute of Technology (RIT).\n\nThis is a **dummy prototype**.\n\nThe application should be extremely simple from the staff\'s perspective.\n\n## 1. Staff Login\n\nCreate a basic staff login page.\n\nUse dummy credentials for now:\n\n```text\nStaff ID: STAFF001\nPassword: staff123\n```\n\nOptionally support:\n\n```text\nSTAFF002 / staff123\nSTAFF003 / staff123\n```\n\nAfter successful login, immediately take the staff member to the staff screen.\n\n---\n\n# 2. Staff Screen \342\200\224 KEEP THIS EXTREMELY SIMPLE\n\nThe staff screen must contain ONLY:\n\n```text\nSTAFF001\n\n[ PUSH ]\n```\n\nThe Staff ID should appear above the button.\n\nThere should be:\n\n* NO navigation bar\n* NO dashboard\n* NO menu\n* NO profile\n* NO history\n* NO location information\n* NO timestamp shown to the staff\n* NO Excel information\n* NO admin controls\n* NO other buttons\n* NO unnecessary text\n\nThe staff member\'s **only action is pressing the PUSH button**.\n\nMake the page clean, centered, and responsive.\n\n---\n\n# 3. Push Button\n\nThe button can be pressed **ONLY ONCE**.\n\nBefore pressing:\n\n```text\nSTAFF001\n\n[ PUSH ]\n```\n\nWhen the staff presses it:\n\n1. Request the browser\'s GPS location.\n2. Obtain latitude and longitude.\n3. Determine which campus location the staff is inside.\n4. Generate the timestamp on the server.\n5. Store the Staff ID, timestamp, latitude, longitude, and detected location in the Excel file.\n6. Change the button to:\n\n```text\n[ PUSHED ]\n```\n\n7. Disable the button permanently for that staff member.\n\nAfter pressing, the screen should simply look like:\n\n```text\nSTAFF001\n\n[ PUSHED ]\n```\n\nThe staff should not be shown any additional information.\n\n---\n\n# 4. Prevent Multiple Pushes\n\nThe system must prevent the same staff member from creating multiple records.\n\nDo NOT rely only on disabling the HTML button.\n\nThe backend must also check whether that Staff ID has already submitted a push.\n\nIf they already submitted one, reject another submission.\n\nFor example:\n\n```text\nSTAFF001 \342\206\222 already recorded\n```\n\nTherefore, only **one Excel record per staff member** should be created in this dummy version.\n\n---\n\n# 5. GPS Location\n\nUse the browser Geolocation API.\n\nExample:\n\n```javascript\nnavigator.geolocation.getCurrentPosition(...)\n```\n\nThe browser should obtain:\n\n```text\nlatitude\nlongitude\n```\n\nThe staff does NOT need to see these coordinates.\n\nThe coordinates should be sent to the Flask backend.\n\n---\n\n# 6. Campus Location Detection\n\nUse the following coordinate ranges from the supplied RIT Campus Coordinate Ranges PDF.\n\nThe PDF specifies:\n\n```text\nLongitude X \342\206\222 Y | Latitude A \342\206\222 B\n```\n\nUse these as bounding ranges for this prototype.\n\n## A / Admin Block\n\n```text\nLongitude: 80.0452290 \342\206\222 80.0457286\nLatitude:  13.0381506 \342\206\222 13.0386278\n```\n\nStore:\n\n```text\nA / Admin Block\n```\n\n## B Block\n\n```text\nLongitude: 80.0448116 \342\206\222 80.0450932\nLatitude:  13.0386850 \342\206\222 13.0394490\n```\n\nStore:\n\n```text\nB Block\n```\n\n## C Blocks (C1\342\200\223C4)\n\n```text\nLongitude: 80.0454785 \342\206\222 80.0459096\nLatitude:  13.0388561 \342\206\222 13.0399281\n```\n\nStore:\n\n```text\nC Blocks (C1\342\200\223C4)\n```\n\n## Steve Jobs\n\n```text\nLongitude: 80.0445206 \342\206\222 80.0448954\nLatitude:  13.0395535 \342\206\222 13.0398507\n```\n\nStore:\n\n```text\nSteve Jobs\n```\n\n## Green Building\n\n```text\nLongitude: 80.0447137 \342\206\222 80.0450191\nLatitude:  13.0377332 \342\206\222 13.0381709\n```\n\nStore:\n\n```text\nGreen Building\n```\n\n## Invisible Statue\n\n```text\nLongitude: 80.0449631 \342\206\222 80.0452458\nLatitude:  13.0396760 \342\206\222 13.0403240\n```\n\nStore:\n\n```text\nInvisible Statue\n```\n\n## Canteen (Bill Counter)\n\n```text\nLongitude: 80.0453383 \342\206\222 80.0454868\nLatitude:  13.0399611 \342\206\222 13.0403701\n```\n\nStore:\n\n```text\nCanteen (Bill Counter)\n```\n\n## Canteen (Calcutta Box)\n\n```text\nLongitude: 80.0452012 \342\206\222 80.0453752\nLatitude:  13.0403335 \342\206\222 13.0405236\n```\n\nStore:\n\n```text\nCanteen (Calcutta Box)\n```\n\n## Outside\n\nIf the latitude and longitude do not fall within any of the above ranges:\n\n```text\nOutside\n```\n\nshould be stored as the location.\n\n---\n\n# 7. Excel File\n\nDo NOT create an admin dashboard yet.\n\nDo NOT create an admin login yet.\n\nDo NOT create an admin page.\n\nFor now, the ONLY requirement is to automatically store the data in an Excel file.\n\nCreate:\n\n```text\nstaff_presence.xlsx\n```\n\nUse Python `openpyxl`.\n\nThe Excel columns must be:\n\n| Staff ID | Timestamp | Latitude | Longitude | Location |\n| -------- | --------- | -------- | --------- | -------- |\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nSTAFF001 | 2026-09-02 21:45:32 | 13.0384 | 80.0454 | A / Admin Block\n```\n\nAnother example if outside:\n\n```text\nSTAFF002 | 2026-09-02 21:51:07 | 13.0412 | 80.0461 | Outside\n```\n\nEvery successful push creates exactly one row.\n\nDo not overwrite existing records.\n\nAppend new records.\n\n---\n\n# 8. Timestamp\n\nThe timestamp must be generated by the **backend/server**, not supplied by the browser.\n\nFormat:\n\n```text\nYYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS\n```\n\nExample:\n\n```text\n2026-09-02 21:45:32\n```\n\nThe timestamp should represent the time at which the staff member successfully pressed the button and their location was recorded.\n\n---\n\n# 9. Location Permission Errors\n\nIf the staff denies GPS permission or GPS cannot be obtained:\n\nDo NOT create an Excel record.\n\nThe button should remain usable so they can try again.\n\nThe staff screen can show only a very small error message if necessary, such as:\n\n```text\nLocation required\n```\n\nDo not show technical GPS information.\n\n---\n\n# 10. Technology\n\nUse:\n\n### Backend\n\n```text\nPython\nFlask\nopenpyxl\n```\n\n### Frontend\n\n```text\nHTML\nCSS\nJavaScript\n```\n\nUse Bootstrap only if useful, but keep the staff interface extremely minimal.\n\n---\n\n# 11. Project Structure\n\nUse a simple structure:\n\n```text\nstaff-location-app/\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 app.py\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 geofence.py\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 requirements.txt\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 staff_presence.xlsx\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 templates/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 login.html\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 staff.html\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 static/\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 style.css\n    \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 staff.js\n```\n\n---\n\n# 12. Application Flow\n\nThe entire application should work like this:\n\n```text\n             STAFF LOGIN\n                  \342\224\202\n                  \342\226\274\n          Enter Staff ID\n          Enter Password\n                  \342\224\202\n                  \342\226\274\n          Successful Login\n                  \342\224\202\n                  \342\226\274\n        \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n        \342\224\202     STAFF001    \342\224\202\n        \342\224\202                 \342\224\202\n        \342\224\202     [ PUSH ]    \342\224\202\n        \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n                 \342\224\202\n                 \342\226\274\n            Get GPS\n                 \342\224\202\n                 \342\226\274\n       Detect Campus Location\n                 \342\224\202\n        \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\264\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n        \342\224\202                 \342\224\202\n     Inside            Outside\n        \342\224\202                 \342\224\202\n        \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n                 \342\224\202\n                 \342\226\274\n       Generate Timestamp\n                 \342\224\202\n                 \342\226\274\n       Save to Excel File\n                 \342\224\202\n                 \342\226\274\n        \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n        \342\224\202     STAFF001    \342\224\202\n        \342\224\202                 \342\224\202\n        \342\224\202    [ PUSHED ]   \342\224\202\n        \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n```\n\n---\n\n# 13. IMPORTANT UI REQUIREMENT\n\nThe staff page is NOT supposed to look like a dashboard.\n\nIt should essentially be a blank page with:\n\n```text\nStaff ID\n\nPUSH button\n```\n\nCenter both vertically and horizontally.\n\nFor example:\n\n```text\n                 STAFF001\n\n\n                 [ PUSH ]\n```\n\nAfter successful submission:\n\n```text\n                 STAFF001\n\n\n                [ PUSHED ]\n```\n\nThe Staff ID is the only information that should remain visible besides the button.\n\nDo not display:\n\n* detected location\n* latitude\n* longitude\n* timestamp\n* Excel status\n* attendance history\n* maps\n* menus\n* admin links\n* logout button\n\nKeep it as a **single-action interface**.\n\n---\n\n# 14. Admin\n\nDO NOT IMPLEMENT ADMIN FUNCTIONALITY YET.\n\nThere should be:\n\n* No admin login\n* No admin dashboard\n* No admin page\n* No admin UI\n\nJust automatically create/update:\n\n```text\nstaff_presence.xlsx\n```\n\nThe Excel file will be handled separately by the person managing the staff.\n\n---\n\n# 15. Important Geofencing Note\n\nThe supplied RIT Campus Coordinate Ranges PDF states that these are KML-derived bounding ranges and that the original KML polygons are more precise than simple coordinate ranges.\n\nFor this prototype, use the coordinate ranges above.\n\nHowever, write the geofencing logic as a separate function/module so that the bounding-box logic can later be replaced with proper KML polygon point-in-polygon detection.\n\nThe location names and coordinate values above must be preserved exactly."
    items {
      text: "# Build a Simple Dummy Staff Push & Location Tracking Web App\n\nCreate a simple full-stack prototype web application for staff presence tracking at Rajalakshmi Institute of Technology (RIT).\n\nThis is a **dummy prototype**.\n\nThe application should be extremely simple from the staff\'s perspective.\n\n## 1. Staff Login\n\nCreate a basic staff login page.\n\nUse dummy credentials for now:\n\n```text\nStaff ID: STAFF001\nPassword: staff123\n```\n\nOptionally support:\n\n```text\nSTAFF002 / staff123\nSTAFF003 / staff123\n```\n\nAfter successful login, immediately take the staff member to the staff screen.\n\n---\n\n# 2. Staff Screen \342\200\224 KEEP THIS EXTREMELY SIMPLE\n\nThe staff screen must contain ONLY:\n\n```text\nSTAFF001\n\n[ PUSH ]\n```\n\nThe Staff ID should appear above the button.\n\nThere should be:\n\n* NO navigation bar\n* NO dashboard\n* NO menu\n* NO profile\n* NO history\n* NO location information\n* NO timestamp shown to the staff\n* NO Excel information\n* NO admin controls\n* NO other buttons\n* NO unnecessary text\n\nThe staff member\'s **only action is pressing the PUSH button**.\n\nMake the page clean, centered, and responsive.\n\n---\n\n# 3. Push Button\n\nThe button can be pressed **ONLY ONCE**.\n\nBefore pressing:\n\n```text\nSTAFF001\n\n[ PUSH ]\n```\n\nWhen the staff presses it:\n\n1. Request the browser\'s GPS location.\n2. Obtain latitude and longitude.\n3. Determine which campus location the staff is inside.\n4. Generate the timestamp on the server.\n5. Store the Staff ID, timestamp, latitude, longitude, and detected location in the Excel file.\n6. Change the button to:\n\n```text\n[ PUSHED ]\n```\n\n7. Disable the button permanently for that staff member.\n\nAfter pressing, the screen should simply look like:\n\n```text\nSTAFF001\n\n[ PUSHED ]\n```\n\nThe staff should not be shown any additional information.\n\n---\n\n# 4. Prevent Multiple Pushes\n\nThe system must prevent the same staff member from creating multiple records.\n\nDo NOT rely only on disabling the HTML button.\n\nThe backend must also check whether that Staff ID has already submitted a push.\n\nIf they already submitted one, reject another submission.\n\nFor example:\n\n```text\nSTAFF001 \342\206\222 already recorded\n```\n\nTherefore, only **one Excel record per staff member** should be created in this dummy version.\n\n---\n\n# 5. GPS Location\n\nUse the browser Geolocation API.\n\nExample:\n\n```javascript\nnavigator.geolocation.getCurrentPosition(...)\n```\n\nThe browser should obtain:\n\n```text\nlatitude\nlongitude\n```\n\nThe staff does NOT need to see these coordinates.\n\nThe coordinates should be sent to the Flask backend.\n\n---\n\n# 6. Campus Location Detection\n\nUse the following coordinate ranges from the supplied RIT Campus Coordinate Ranges PDF.\n\nThe PDF specifies:\n\n```text\nLongitude X \342\206\222 Y | Latitude A \342\206\222 B\n```\n\nUse these as bounding ranges for this prototype.\n\n## A / Admin Block\n\n```text\nLongitude: 80.0452290 \342\206\222 80.0457286\nLatitude:  13.0381506 \342\206\222 13.0386278\n```\n\nStore:\n\n```text\nA / Admin Block\n```\n\n## B Block\n\n```text\nLongitude: 80.0448116 \342\206\222 80.0450932\nLatitude:  13.0386850 \342\206\222 13.0394490\n```\n\nStore:\n\n```text\nB Block\n```\n\n## C Blocks (C1\342\200\223C4)\n\n```text\nLongitude: 80.0454785 \342\206\222 80.0459096\nLatitude:  13.0388561 \342\206\222 13.0399281\n```\n\nStore:\n\n```text\nC Blocks (C1\342\200\223C4)\n```\n\n## Steve Jobs\n\n```text\nLongitude: 80.0445206 \342\206\222 80.0448954\nLatitude:  13.0395535 \342\206\222 13.0398507\n```\n\nStore:\n\n```text\nSteve Jobs\n```\n\n## Green Building\n\n```text\nLongitude: 80.0447137 \342\206\222 80.0450191\nLatitude:  13.0377332 \342\206\222 13.0381709\n```\n\nStore:\n\n```text\nGreen Building\n```\n\n## Invisible Statue\n\n```text\nLongitude: 80.0449631 \342\206\222 80.0452458\nLatitude:  13.0396760 \342\206\222 13.0403240\n```\n\nStore:\n\n```text\nInvisible Statue\n```\n\n## Canteen (Bill Counter)\n\n```text\nLongitude: 80.0453383 \342\206\222 80.0454868\nLatitude:  13.0399611 \342\206\222 13.0403701\n```\n\nStore:\n\n```text\nCanteen (Bill Counter)\n```\n\n## Canteen (Calcutta Box)\n\n```text\nLongitude: 80.0452012 \342\206\222 80.0453752\nLatitude:  13.0403335 \342\206\222 13.0405236\n```\n\nStore:\n\n```text\nCanteen (Calcutta Box)\n```\n\n## Outside\n\nIf the latitude and longitude do not fall within any of the above ranges:\n\n```text\nOutside\n```\n\nshould be stored as the location.\n\n---\n\n# 7. Excel File\n\nDo NOT create an admin dashboard yet.\n\nDo NOT create an admin login yet.\n\nDo NOT create an admin page.\n\nFor now, the ONLY requirement is to automatically store the data in an Excel file.\n\nCreate:\n\n```text\nstaff_presence.xlsx\n```\n\nUse Python `openpyxl`.\n\nThe Excel columns must be:\n\n| Staff ID | Timestamp | Latitude | Longitude | Location |\n| -------- | --------- | -------- | --------- | -------- |\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nSTAFF001 | 2026-09-02 21:45:32 | 13.0384 | 80.0454 | A / Admin Block\n```\n\nAnother example if outside:\n\n```text\nSTAFF002 | 2026-09-02 21:51:07 | 13.0412 | 80.0461 | Outside\n```\n\nEvery successful push creates exactly one row.\n\nDo not overwrite existing records.\n\nAppend new records.\n\n---\n\n# 8. Timestamp\n\nThe timestamp must be generated by the **backend/server**, not supplied by the browser.\n\nFormat:\n\n```text\nYYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS\n```\n\nExample:\n\n```text\n2026-09-02 21:45:32\n```\n\nThe timestamp should represent the time at which the staff member successfully pressed the button and their location was recorded.\n\n---\n\n# 9. Location Permission Errors\n\nIf the staff denies GPS permission or GPS cannot be obtained:\n\nDo NOT create an Excel record.\n\nThe button should remain usable so they can try again.\n\nThe staff screen can show only a very small error message if necessary, such as:\n\n```text\nLocation required\n```\n\nDo not show technical GPS information.\n\n---\n\n# 10. Technology\n\nUse:\n\n### Backend\n\n```text\nPython\nFlask\nopenpyxl\n```\n\n### Frontend\n\n```text\nHTML\nCSS\nJavaScript\n```\n\nUse Bootstrap only if useful, but keep the staff interface extremely minimal.\n\n---\n\n# 11. Project Structure\n\nUse a simple structure:\n\n```text\nstaff-location-app/\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 app.py\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 geofence.py\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 requirements.txt\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 staff_presence.xlsx\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 templates/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 login.html\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 staff.html\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 static/\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 style.css\n    \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 staff.js\n```\n\n---\n\n# 12. Application Flow\n\nThe entire application should work like this:\n\n```text\n             STAFF LOGIN\n                  \342\224\202\n                  \342\226\274\n          Enter Staff ID\n          Enter Password\n                  \342\224\202\n                  \342\226\274\n          Successful Login\n                  \342\224\202\n                  \342\226\274\n        \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n        \342\224\202     STAFF001    \342\224\202\n        \342\224\202                 \342\224\202\n        \342\224\202     [ PUSH ]    \342\224\202\n        \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n                 \342\224\202\n                 \342\226\274\n            Get GPS\n                 \342\224\202\n                 \342\226\274\n       Detect Campus Location\n                 \342\224\202\n        \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\264\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n        \342\224\202                 \342\224\202\n     Inside            Outside\n        \342\224\202                 \342\224\202\n        \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n                 \342\224\202\n                 \342\226\274\n       Generate Timestamp\n                 \342\224\202\n                 \342\226\274\n       Save to Excel File\n                 \342\224\202\n                 \342\226\274\n        \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n        \342\224\202     STAFF001    \342\224\202\n        \342\224\202                 \342\224\202\n        \342\224\202    [ PUSHED ]   \342\224\202\n        \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n```\n\n---\n\n# 13. IMPORTANT UI REQUIREMENT\n\nThe staff page is NOT supposed to look like a dashboard.\n\nIt should essentially be a blank page with:\n\n```text\nStaff ID\n\nPUSH button\n```\n\nCenter both vertically and horizontally.\n\nFor example:\n\n```text\n                 STAFF001\n\n\n                 [ PUSH ]\n```\n\nAfter successful submission:\n\n```text\n                 STAFF001\n\n\n                [ PUSHED ]\n```\n\nThe Staff ID is the only information that should remain visible besides the button.\n\nDo not display:\n\n* detected location\n* latitude\n* longitude\n* timestamp\n* Excel status\n* attendance history\n* maps\n* menus\n* admin links\n* logout button\n\nKeep it as a **single-action interface**.\n\n---\n\n# 14. Admin\n\nDO NOT IMPLEMENT ADMIN FUNCTIONALITY YET.\n\nThere should be:\n\n* No admin login\n* No admin dashboard\n* No admin page\n* No admin UI\n\nJust automatically create/update:\n\n```text\nstaff_presence.xlsx\n```\n\nThe Excel file will be handled separately by the person managing the staff.\n\n---\n\n# 15. Important Geofencing Note\n\nThe supplied RIT Campus Coordinate Ranges PDF states that these are KML-derived bounding ranges and that the original KML polygons are more precise than simple coordinate ranges.\n\nFor this prototype, use the coordinate ranges above.\n\nHowever, write the geofencing logic as a separate function/module so that the bounding-box logic can later be replaced with proper KML polygon point-in-polygon detection.\n\nThe location names and coordinate values above must be preserved exactly."
