    thinking: "**Defining Backend Needs**\n\nOkay, so I\'m honing in on the backend requirements. I need it to handle server-side timestamp generation in the `YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS` format. Plus, GPS coordinates validation is a must. And, of course, location geofencing with exact coordinate ranges from the prompt, which needs to be modular.\n\n\n**Outlining API Endpoints**\n\nNow I\'m diving into the API structure. I\'ve sketched out `/api/login` for staff authentication and `/api/push` to handle the location data. There\'s also a `/api/status` endpoint to check push status and persist push records (with appropriate error handling). I need to prevent duplicate pushes efficiently, and the `staff_presence.xlsx` file will be updated with the provided data.\n\n\n**Constructing Deployment Strategy**\n\nI\'m now detailing the deployment process, thinking through the build process. I\'m focusing on creating an Express-backed web preview in AI Studio, deploying the Node.js server with bundling, and generating the necessary Python Flask files for local execution. My goal is to ensure both immediate online usability and a runnable local version. Also verifying the geofence logic in both TypeScript and Python.\n\n\n"
