  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the UI**\n\nOkay, I\'m now focusing on the UI design within `src/App.tsx`. The goal is a clean, professional login screen for the initial, not-logged-in state. This includes a Staff ID input field. I\'m visualizing how this will render in the Google AI Studio live preview.\n\n\n**Refining the Staff Screen**\n\nI\'ve got the staff screen requirements nailed down. It\'s incredibly minimal \342\200\223 just the Staff ID and a \"PUSH\" button. I\'m focusing on the \"PUSH\" functionality, including disabling the button after the action, and considering how to gracefully handle the case where GPS permission is denied. I am working on the button state after submission.\n\n\n**Simplifying the Staff Screen**\n\nI\'ve stripped the staff screen down to its bare essentials: just the Staff ID and a \"PUSH\" button, centered both vertically and horizontally. After submission, the button will change to \"PUSHED\", with the Staff ID remaining visible. I\'ve confirmed no other elements are needed, including error messages limited to \"Location required\" if necessary. Testing and reset will be handled via keyboard shortcut or session storage, ensuring the UI stays focused. I\'ve verified geolocation permissions.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 273895165
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
