    }
    tool_summary: "Create comprehensive README documentation"
    tool_action: "Create README.md"
    started_at {
      seconds: 1788366661
      nanos: 313257882
    }
  }
  file_change {
    absolute_path_uri: "file:///README.md"
    file_change_type: FILE_CHANGE_TYPE_CREATE
    replacement_chunks {
      replacement_content: "# RIT Staff Location Attendance Web App (Dummy Prototype)\n\nA prototype dummy web application for staff location-based attendance tracking for **Rajalakshmi Institute of Technology (RIT)**.\n\n## Key Features\n\n1. **Staff Login**:\n   - Hardcoded dummy credentials for prototype demonstration.\n   - Credentials:\n     - `STAFF001` / `staff123`\n     - `STAFF002` / `staff123`\n     - `STAFF003` / `staff123`\n\n2. **Ultra-Minimal Staff Screen**:\n   - Shows **only** the logged-in Staff ID and a single **`[ PUSH ]`** button.\n   - Clean, centered vertically and horizontally.\n   - No menus, no navigation bar, no dashboard, no history, no visible coordinates or timestamps.\n\n3. **Single-Action Geofence Recording**:\n   - On pressing **`[ PUSH ]`**, the browser requests GPS coordinates (`navigator.geolocation`).\n   - The backend validates coordinates against the defined RIT campus bounding ranges.\n   - If within a campus block, records that specific block name. If outside campus ranges, records `Outside`.\n   - Server-side timestamp generated in `YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS` format.\n   - Appends record to `staff_presence.xlsx` with columns:\n     `Staff ID | Timestamp | Latitude | Longitude | Location`\n   - Visually changes button to **`[ PUSHED ]`** and disables it permanently.\n   - Server-side duplicate prevention ensures a staff member can only push once.\n\n---\n\n## Campus Geofence Zones\n\nDerived from the RIT Campus Coordinate Ranges specification (`Longitude X -> Y | Latitude A -> B`):\n\n1. **A / Admin Block**:\n   - Longitude: `80.0452290` \342\206\222 `80.0457286`\n   - Latitude: `13.0381506` \342\206\222 `13.0386278`\n2. **B Block**:\n   - Longitude: `80.0448116` \342\206\222 `80.0450932`\n   - Latitude: `13.0386850` \342\206\222 `13.0394490`\n3. **C Blocks (C1\342\200\223C4)**:\n   - Longitude: `80.0454785` \342\206\222 `80.0459096`\n   - Latitude: `13.0388561` \342\206\222 `13.0399281`\n4. **Steve Jobs**:\n   - Longitude: `80.0445206` \342\206\222 `80.0448954`\n   - Latitude: `13.0395535` \342\206\222 `13.0398507`\n5. **Green Building**:\n   - Longitude: `80.0447137` \342\206\222 `80.0450191`\n   - Latitude: `13.0377332` \342\206\222 `13.0381709`\n6. **Invisible Statue**:\n   - Longitude: `80.0449631` \342\206\222 `80.0452458`\n   - Latitude: `13.0396760` \342\206\222 `13.0403240`\n7. **Canteen (Bill Counter)**:\n   - Longitude: `80.0453383` \342\206\222 `80.0454868`\n   - Latitude: `13.0399611` \342\206\222 `13.0403701`\n8. **Canteen (Calcutta Box)**:\n   - Longitude: `80.0452012` \342\206\222 `80.0453752`\n   - Latitude: `13.0403335` \342\206\222 `13.0405236`\n9. **Outside**: Any coordinate not matching the above.\n\n*Note: The geofencing logic is isolated in `geofence.py` (and `src/geofence.ts`) so bounding-box logic can easily be substituted with polygon point-in-polygon checks in the future.*\n\n---\n\n## Running Locally\n\n### Option A: Python Flask Backend\n\n1. Install requirements:\n   ```bash\n   pip install -r requirements.txt\n   ```\n\n2. Run the application:\n   ```bash\n   python app.py\n   ```\n\n3. Open your browser at `http://localhost:3000`.\n\n### Option B: Node.js / Express & React\n\n1. Install dependencies:\n   ```bash\n   npm install\n   ```\n\n2. Start the dev server:\n   ```bash\n   npm run dev\n   ```\n\n3. Open your browser at `http://localhost:3000`.\n\n---\n\n## Excel Output\n\nGenerated file: `staff_presence.xlsx`\n\n| Staff ID | Timestamp | Latitude | Longitude | Location |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| STAFF001 | 2026-09-02 21:45:32 | 13.038421 | 80.045412 | A / Admin Block |\n| STAFF002 | 2026-09-02 21:51:07 | 13.041200 | 80.046100 | Outside |\n\n---\n\n## Demo Credentials Note\n\n> **DISCLAIMER:** The hardcoded credentials are for prototype and demonstration purposes only. A production deployment must integrate proper institutional authentication (SSO / OAuth / Active Directory), encrypted passwords, and secure database storage.\n"
    }
